Use io and string.

Define function generate taking open_count as an unsigned number, close_count as an unsigned number, n as an unsigned number, buffer as a pointer to byte, depth as an unsigned number:
    If depth equals n * 2:
        Let answer be create text from buffer of length depth.
        Say answer.
        str_free(address of answer).
        Give back.
    If open_count is less than n:
        Set item depth of buffer to 40.
        generate(open_count + 1, close_count, n, buffer, depth + 1).
    If close_count is less than open_count:
        Set item depth of buffer to 41.
        generate(open_count, close_count + 1, n, buffer, depth + 1).
Done.

Let n be 3.
Let buffer be block of 16 byte.
generate(0 as an unsigned number, 0 as an unsigned number, n as an unsigned number, address of item 0 of buffer, 0 as an unsigned number).
Return 0.
